--- virtualenv -
--activators=	the activators to generate (comma-separated; default: all supported)
--always-copy 	try to use copies rather than symlinks, even when symlinks are the default for the
--app-data=	a data folder used as cache by the virtualenv
--clear 	remove the destination directory if exist before starting (will overwrite files otherwise)
--copies 	try to use copies rather than symlinks, even when symlinks are the default for the
--creator=	create the environment with (builtin: cpython3-posix)
--discovery=	interpreter discovery method
--download 	download the latest pip/setuptools/wheel from PyPI
--extra-search-dir=	a path containing wheels to extend the internal wheel list (can be set 1+ times)
--never-download 	don't download the latest pip/setuptools/wheel from PyPI
--no-download 	don't download the latest pip/setuptools/wheel from PyPI
--no-periodic-update 	disable the periodic (once every 14 days) update of the embedded wheels
--no-pip 	do not install pip
--no-seed 	do not install seed packages
--no-setuptools 	do not install setuptools
--no-vcs-ignore 	don't create VCS ignore directive in the destination directory
--no-venv-redirect 	write no PEP-832 .venv redirect file
--pip=	version of pip to install as seed: embed, bundle, none or exact version
--prompt=	an alternative prompt prefix for the environment (.: the name of the current directory)
--read-only-app-data 	use app data folder in read-only mode (write operations will fail with error)
--reset-app-data 	start with empty app data folder
--seeder=	seed packages install method
--setuptools=	version of setuptools to install as seed: embed, bundle, none or exact version
--symlink-app-data 	symlink the python packages from the app-data folder
--symlinks 	try to use symlinks rather than copies, when symlinks are not the default for the platform
--system-site-packages 	give the virtual environment access to the system site-packages dir
--try-first-with=	try first these interpreters before starting the discovery
--upgrade-embed-wheels 	trigger a manual update of the embedded wheels
--venv-redirect 	point a PEP-832 .venv redirect file next to the destination at the created environment
--version 	display the version of the virtualenv package and its location, then exit
--with-traceback 	on failure also display the stacktrace internals of virtualenv
--without-pip 	do not install seed packages
-h 	show this help message and exit
-p 	the interpreter to create the environment with
-q 	decrease verbosity
-v 	increase verbosity
